{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests","id":1445490,"title":"Victorian Mage expansion ideas/requests","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-23T10:04:58-07:00","id":1445490,"title":"Victorian Mage expansion ideas/requests","content":"I am working on a Companion for Victorian Mage for the Storyteller's Vault (obviously there may be revisions to what I'm covering if the final pdf turns out to be notably different than the manuscript preview, but I'm starting writing now). There are some topics I have a lot to say on, but I realize some Traditions are looking at less coverage than others because I have less to add, so I thought I'd see if other people have particular topics they'd like to see addressed/expanded on, or even things they'd be interested in collaborating on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T10:45:18-07:00","id":1445498,"title":"","content":"Mount Qaf. As I said elsewhere, this is something that is a non-issue after it's destruction or loss at the start of the 20th century, and possibly wasn't a big deal at some point early on in Batini history. But if it was ever as important as the Batini claim it was the Victorian era would be when it was at its height of importance. So I'd like to see something addressing Mount Qaf; specifically, how do you go there, why do you go there, and what can you do when you're there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:36:47-07:00","id":1445517,"title":"","content":"I could probably think of a bunch of stuff off the top of my head, but it will take me a bit to fully gather my thoughts.<br /> <br /> But just to start, a look at Transylvania/Romania as a potential crossover setting with Victorian Vampire, as well as local members of the Verbena, Celestial Chorus, Euthanatos, Dreamspeakers, and such would be interesting. (Possibly also Hermetics and what ever happened to the old Tremere strongholds in the region as a sidebar.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T10:39:52-07:00","id":1445686,"title":"","content":"(With the caveat that I've no idea exactly what Victorian Mage specifically covers and in what detail.)<br /> <br /> Two things:<br /> <br /> Hawaii (and possibly the rest of Polynesia). I mentioned this one in my Ages of Darkness thread, as it is the transition period when Hawaii was an independent kingdom (and something of a client state of the British) before eventually being overthrown by American business interests. Besides the fact that its a place where a number of Traditions (East, West, and Native) can exist together, and a potentially interesting place for the Technocracy, it's also a great reason to discuss the Kopa Loei craft and what they are doing during the time period. <br /> <br /> First Wave Feminism. Growing out of the 18th century works of people like Mary Wollstonecraft (the mother of the author of Frankenstein), Judith Sargent Murray, and others, and from the organization of the abolitionist movement, this is the era of people like Elizabeth Cady Stanton, Susan B. Anthony, Victoria Woodhull, Matilda Gage, Sojourner Truth, and many others advocating for women's suffrage, changes to divorce, property and inheritance laws, and the ability to attend certain types of higher education. This ties in with various changes to the medical establishment, with Florence Nightingale'a efforts to overhaul the practice of nursing and other aspects of hospital management, and the first recognized women medical doctors. Also the Temperance Movement, female missionaries, and other religious issues, and the continuing tradition of women scientists from the Enlightenment Era. This sort of thing ties in with almost all of the female centric/exclusive sub-factions within the Traditions (such as the Sisterhood of Gabrielle and the Kiss of Astarte), especially the Verbena. Also the Sisters of Hippolyta. <br /> <br /> <br /> (Honestly, it'd be kind of amusing the have a Victorian Mage sourcebook entirely based around the original Book of Crafts, looking at things like Egypt and the post-Napoleonic Egyptology fad, Christianity in the 19th century, Victorian era pharmaceuticals and apothecaries, the First Wave Feminist movement, the Chinese Diaspora and European imperialism in China, the Kingdom of Hawaii and other Polynesian regions/cultures, and the Afro-Caribbean/Afro-Brazilian cultures of places like Haiti and the Empire of Brazil. Maybe also some of the original WoD: Sorcerer stuff with West Africa, the Mormons, what's going on in the Yucatan and Central America, the Order of the Golden Dawn, and possibly Theosophy as a forerunner of the Thal'hun.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T13:29:51-07:00","id":1445705,"title":"","content":"Actually, that's not a bad idea as an organizing principle for the book call it each chapter deals with one faction (usually, but not necessarily, a craft) along with one related subject matter. I wouldn't limit it to the crafts from the original Book of Crafts; though that's a good starting point. <br /> <br /> And with that in mind, I would also like to see something done concerning the other Enlightened Scientists of Africa that were briefly mentioned in the manuscript but not detailed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T17:28:48-07:00","id":1445749,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Do the Lions of Zion and talk about the state of Judaism in the era, including the origins of Zionism, the Dreyfus affair and antisemitism (especially in France). The Ngoma maybe discuss the state of what is now South Africa and its various ethnic and cultural groups. <br /> <br /> <br /> Beyond that, the other planets in the solar system and what they look like from the perspective of Victorian science fiction and speculation, and how that might influence the Umbral versions of the Moon, Mars, Venus, and Mercury. Also the theorized planet Vulcan. Also the various ways to actually get their, including stuff like Verne's Gun Club, Wells's Cavorite, and others. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T11:07:17-07:00","id":1445847,"title":"","content":"I don't remember the Lions of Zion being mentioned. There's been a few issues with the Craft since they were introduced. There's been a whole lot of talk over social media to get an Umbra treatment for VA Mage, as well. One thing I'm trying to get my head around is how the Shard Realms were treated before their physical planet counterparts were &quot;discovered&quot; by mundane science. Was there a Pluto before the 1930s? And think about this, Uranus can technically seen by the naked eye or with basic optics, but ancient observers never even considered the possibility of another planet. I think that someone could have. Even if not, the seeds of a story are planted. I would also like to see how much the Umbra has changed/is different from the modern era. The Middle Umbra Near Realms would be much the same, as would the Underworld. The High Umbra might have undergone a previous change though. My own personal theories on the Umbra have been developing along such wide tangents as well.<br /> <br /> There should also be a deeper dive into Hedge magicians. With the high degree of occult societies around, I would think there would be a greater number of sorcerers and the like. Many paths and practices would be slightly different than today's. More of these smaller groups could also be a focus for Crafts, especially the budding Hollow Ones. This would also be one of the last great ages for Bygones. With such strong themes of exploration and colonialism, the need for a last great exodus wold be a great theme. One last look at these being before leaving earth as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T11:59:11-07:00","id":1445852,"title":"","content":"Some of the (many) wars of the period include;<ul><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eighth_Xhosa_War\" target=\"_blank\">Eighth Xhosa War</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiping_Rebellion\" target=\"_blank\">Taiping Rebellion</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_Indian_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">California Indian Wars</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimean_War\" target=\"_blank\">Crimean War</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bleeding_Kansas\" target=\"_blank\">Bleeding Kansas</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seminole_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">Seminole Wars</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Persian_War\" target=\"_blank\">Anglo-Persian War</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War\" target=\"_blank\">American Civil War</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_Uprising\" target=\"_blank\">January Uprising</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franco-Prussian_War\" target=\"_blank\">Franco-Prussian War</a></li> </ul><br /> The era was rife with wars, many of them with long lasting consequences and many of them seeing a clash between what might broadly be called a technocractic warfair style and other forms of conflict. Any such war might suck in the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T12:15:32-07:00","id":1445853,"title":"","content":"Right. It wasn't just an era of social transformation, it was also one of technological change as well. Just in the American civil war, we got the first ironclads. If Victorian mage and it's supplement don't end up covering this sort of thing, it wouldn't hurt to give a rundown of what the state of the arts in the 19th century was like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T16:37:14-07:00","id":1445888,"title":"","content":"The Victorians tried to build multiple Utopian comunities. This wasn't only a US thing. A small supplement on utopian projects, what kind of people built them and where would have serious gaming possibilities. <br /> <br /> Since areas of lower population densities with less Technocratic influence would have weaker or no paradox, maps of which areas of the USA had what level of paradox when would be very gamable. As an example, New Orleans would have had lower paradox than New York City or Philadelphia, with some of the nearby bayous being paradox free up until after the civil war. Large areas of the Apilachians and Ozarks would have been paradox free into the early 20th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T20:42:00-07:00","id":1445918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1445888#post1445888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Victorians tried to build multiple Utopian comunities. This wasn't only a US thing. A small supplement on utopian projects, what kind of people built them and where would have serious gaming possibilities. <br /> <br /> Since areas of lower population densities with less Technocratic influence would have weaker or no paradox, maps of which areas of the USA had what level of paradox when would be very gamable. As an example, New Orleans would have had lower paradox than New York City or Philadelphia, with some of the nearby bayous being paradox free up until after the civil war. Large areas of the Apilachians and Ozarks would have been paradox free into the early 20th century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well nowhere is paradox free. It\u2019s a question of what did or did not defy the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T00:52:24-07:00","id":1445941,"title":"","content":"The British Raj.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T04:15:33-07:00","id":1445949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1445941#post1445941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The British Raj.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magnificent idea! The possibilities from adventure stories to complex social dramas are vast. You also have the drama of competing visions of the good. Historically some British colonial actions were welcomed by the locals. The struggle against the Thugs is still celebrated in India as is the banning of Widow burning. Meanwhile the forced changes in agricultural practices created vast famines. In all these cases people of more or less good will come into disasterous conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T07:50:07-07:00","id":1445968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1445918#post1445918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well nowhere is paradox free. It\u2019s a question of what did or did not defy the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I think parts of the Victorian era world would favor different paradigms, such as what might be called a Verbena paradigm or a Dreamspeaker paradigm and so on. But no region would be free of consensus and paradox. And my the end of the era the technocratic paradigm is ascendant world wide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T08:18:45-07:00","id":1445973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1445941#post1445941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The British Raj.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an overview in the gazateer chapter currently, but I will be expanding on it with the Chorus, Ecstatic, and Euthanatoi chapters - as all three of those traditions break in half between their European and Indian factions in 1857, and reconciliation takes a bit.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m taking a similar route with the \u201cThuggee\u201d that I do with the European Witch Trials in Sorcerer\u2019s Crusade - there is no secret truth behind the events recorded in mortal history - the Brits were labeling unrelated rebels and generic bandits with the term in order to invent a boogeyman that largely was not there. HOWEVER, the Order of Reason used the cover of that crack down to go after the Chakravanti. A less corrupt Voormas will cameo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-26-2021, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T17:09:10-07:00","id":1446006,"title":"","content":"(Again with the above caveat)<br /> <br /> The origins of modern professional police forces and how they work. Probably also the flip side of criminals and crime in the period. <br /> <br /> How high society staples like private clubs, dinner and garden parties, social calling, and the like work, and their importance to how things get done at that tier of society. Also how these things differ in Britain, France, the US, and the like. (Also the parallels between similar customs in Japan, China, the Ottoman Empire, and elsewhere.) <br /> <br /> Spiritualism and psychical research in the Victorian period. <br /> <br /> All of the various ritual magic/occult societies like the Golden Dawn, the Rosicrucians, and so forth. <br /> <br /> Victorian Era Bygones. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T21:20:00-07:00","id":1446044,"title":"","content":"The Australian Frontier Wars and Massacres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T14:38:03-07:00","id":1446661,"title":"","content":"I would like a book dedicated to the Science, Technology and Technomancy of the era. A Victorian counterpart ot MtSC's Artisan's Handbook.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T15:03:14-07:00","id":1446665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1446661#post1446661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like a book dedicated to the Science, Technology and Technomancy of the era. A Victorian counterpart ot MtSC's Artisan's Handbook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm writing the Order of Reason chapter currently, and in addition to era tech like the HIT Mark IIIs, enlightened Difference Engines, electromagnetic shielding and weapons, etc etc I also put major focus on exploring how Malthus, Galton, and Spencer shape the dominant biological and social paradigm of the elites of the English speaking world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:28:31-07:00","id":1446695,"title":"","content":"If it hasn't been mentioned earlier, we need culture/society books on at least the USA and England (Scotland, Wales, and Ireland are parts of the UK in this period, but very different from England and deserving of their own books). After those two, France, Germany, the Ottoman Empire, Japan, and China, would all be grand. And given how rare any RPG information on Indonesia is, a book on the Dutch East Indies would be golden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T19:12:43-07:00","id":1446715,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I've looked into the subject, but IIRC, after he built his first Difference Engine (in the 1820s, I think), Babbage made theoretical designs for the next step, the Analytical Engine, but never actually constructed one. The Analytical Engine was meant to be a general purpose computer, complete with integrated memory and other functions (I think the modern term is Turing-complete, but my computer knowledge has atrophied too much over the past decade to fully grok all of it), where as the Difference Engine is a mechanical calculator. They're supposed to be what the Analytical Reckoners (the group that comes in between the Difference Engineers and the Virtual Adepts) are named after. <br /> (I've long had this image in my head of 19th century Analytical Reckoners running around with talisman analytical engines that fit in briefcases and make use of early theories of wireless telegraphy. Probably using it to connect to larger engines kept back at their chantry.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T21:09:59-07:00","id":1446727,"title":"","content":"In doing research for the MtAs game i am planning, I discovered the Syndicate accidentally created Pentex - the evil company that manufactures evil - in the 1890s. So that happens during this period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T21:52:01-07:00","id":1446739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1446727#post1446727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In doing research for the MtAs game i am planning, I discovered the Syndicate accidentally created Pentex - the evil company that manufactures evil - in the 1890s. So that happens during this period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a source on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T22:18:32-07:00","id":1446744,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Special_Projects_Division_(MTAs)\" target=\"_blank\">Special Projects Division</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T23:17:53-07:00","id":1446749,"title":"","content":"Specifically, <b>Technocracy: Syndicate</b> p.36.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T01:19:26-07:00","id":1446755,"title":"","content":"Is it wrong I really-really can't wait for the Kindle version of the Victorian Vampire Trilogy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It and Penny Dreadful are great rewards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T02:11:58-07:00","id":1446759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1445853#post1445853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. It wasn't just an era of social transformation, it was also one of technological change as well. Just in the American civil war, we got the first ironclads. If Victorian mage and it's supplement don't end up covering this sort of thing, it wouldn't hurt to give a rundown of what the state of the arts in the 19th century was like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends when in the 19th century you are. Is the default start 1880, like in Victorian Vampire? <br /> <br /> Because the difference between, say 1810 and 1880 is enormous. It's like the difference between 1900 and 1970.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T07:22:46-07:00","id":1446792,"title":"","content":"Victorian Mage covers a lot more ground than Victorian Vampire did. From what I gather, VV not only focuses heavily on just the tail end of the 19th century, but also tends to focus on Britain. Victorian Mage effectively starts around the 1830s and goes right up to the turn of the century; it also goes global. <br /> <br /> And yes, the difference is huge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:31:31-07:00","id":1447228,"title":"","content":"Victorian fashion and clothing, including how people of various social classes were expected to dress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:54:59-07:00","id":1447233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1447228#post1447228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Victorian fashion and clothing, including how people of various social classes were expected to dress.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want to focus on things people can't just look up themselves - i.e. Mage society, how it intersects with important events in sleeper history, the Paradigmatic elements of the era and rotes, etc. I'm using public domain illustrations and photos from the era for the books' art though, so that will hopefully help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T11:01:11-07:00","id":1447235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1446759#post1446759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends when in the 19th century you are. Is the default start 1880, like in Victorian Vampire?<br /> <br /> Because the difference between, say 1810 and 1880 is enormous. It's like the difference between 1900 and 1970.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Victorian Mage nominally covers the whole of Victoria's reign from 1837-1901, but puts it's main focus on the window between the Albertan Reformation (1851) and the Victorian Reformation (beginning in 1885 but culminating in 1897) that created the modern Technocratic Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-03-2021, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T12:30:52-07:00","id":1447244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1447233#post1447233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I want to focus on things people can't just look up themselves - i.e. Mage society, how it intersects with important events in sleeper history, the Paradigmatic elements of the era and rotes, etc. I'm using public domain illustrations and photos from the era for the books' art though, so that will hopefully help.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you end up talking about class distinctions, I vaguely recall a skit involving three men: there was a picture from it, with them lined up from tallest to shortest, each looking down on the one next to him. This was figurative as well as literal, does the first was an upper class man, the second was working class, and the third was\u2026 well, I don't quite recall; but you get the idea. Where I saw this, it was pointed out to me the hats that each of them was wearing, and how their choices of hats reflected their station.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T12:35:44-07:00","id":1447245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1447228#post1447228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Victorian fashion and clothing, including how people of various social classes were expected to dress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call, I remember a four page note on that in a Victorian supplement to Call of Cthulhu. And much of the space was illustrations. We don't need much, but we need something. And maybe the title of a book or two for those who want more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T20:11:15-07:00","id":1447320,"title":"","content":"I would like a Sons of Ether version of the Echoes flaw: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440156-please-help-me-construct-an-etherite-specific-version-of-the-echoes-flaw\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...he-echoes-flaw</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T18:30:30-07:00","id":1447876,"title":"","content":"Maybe Spiritualism and how it applies to Euthanatos, Dreamspeakers, (proto)Hollow Ones, and others. <br /> <br /> Drugs in the 19th century and how that sort of thing may (or may not) apply to the Cult of Ecstasy. (And possibly the Children of Knowledge.) <br /> <br /> Pluto hasn't been discovered yet. I'm not sure what impact that would have on astrology, it's Umbral reflection, and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T04:16:59-07:00","id":1447922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1447244#post1447244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you end up talking about class distinctions, I vaguely recall a skit involving three men: there was a picture from it, with them lined up from tallest to shortest, each looking down on the one next to him. This was figurative as well as literal, does the first was an upper class man, the second was working class, and the third was\u2026 well, I don't quite recall; but you get the idea. Where I saw this, it was pointed out to me the hats that each of them was wearing, and how their choices of hats reflected their station.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> this is the original of it, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C4HflC2L7M4\" target=\"_blank\">Social Class sketch The Frost Report 1966</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Also on the original topic I'd say a city/region book would be a good thing, something to give a setting and a flavour of the era, with the structures and so forth worked out, so can just drop the characters into a space that doesn't need to much prep work by the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","user":"babi_gog","date":". 05-08-2021, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T17:12:43-07:00","id":1448636,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see Rathbone's Skeleton Keys explored more thoroughly, and Victoria's specific role as a patron of the Technocratic Union. Since I've been going on a Victorian history kick lately, I have a few ideas on things that could be explored. Forgive any canon errors on my part, as I don't have the books currently at hand, and this is based entirely off of some ideas that I was kicking around a bit over a month ago. I'll start with my favorite Tradition-to-be. I'll probably post more later if I'm not actively discouraged from doing so.<br /> <br /> The Society Of Ether is still within the Technocracy as the Electrodyne Engineers, but since that link finally dissolves shortly after the turn of the century, we're going to be seeing lines of communication opening up with the Traditions as the Victorian Age progresses further towards imposing an ever-narrowing paradigm on every part of the world touched by the British Empire, and beyond. The Convention (and future Tradition) is likely characterized by enormous levels of intrigue, fierce debate between those who wish to work within the Technocracy and those who think that it's time to forge a different path, and growing alienation from the rest of their Technocratic colleagues as Paradox causes their sky ships to burst into flames, their steam-powered death rays to explode in their faces, and their own patchwork creations to turn upon them in their hidden laboratories. Never the most trusting types, paranoia likely runs rampant through their laboratory chantries. It's almost certain that an Etherite character will be forced to pick one side or another. Of course, it's entirely possible that the character will try to remain above the fray in order to focus on their research, but a moment of crisis is coming, and friends may be thin on the ground for those who go their own way.<br /> <br /> You obviously have the traditional mad scientist types, steampunk engineers, and Jules Verne's would-be conquerors, but also patent medicine creators, idealistic Yankee inventors, ingenious blacksmiths, and itinerant peddlers of miracle gadgets and electrical toys. More grimly, the Engineers are almost certainly among the colonizing forces, using steam-powered automatic cannons and clockwork soldiers against the native cultures, particularly when &quot;local&quot; magic is involved. The Science Adventure stories of the time, of course, portray all of this in the most heroic of lights.<br /> <br /> The number of science fiction tropes created during the era are obviously to numerous to count, and I'm not going to insult anyone's intelligence by going into detail on them. Suffice to say that anyone reading this probably has a sufficient familiarity with the material, or at least knows where to look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T08:33:40-07:00","id":1448693,"title":"","content":"One element of Victorian society that may be worth a mention is the club system. With a few disreputable exceptions, nearly early every male Londoner of the upper middle class and above belonged to some club or another where he could congregate with people of like status, interest, or occupation, and women began to form their own, similar clubs later in the century. These organizations served not just a social purpose, but also provided opportunities for professional networking, political maneuvering, and information brokering. To the best of my immediate recollection, middle-class Londoners had their own organizations based more upon common hobbies, political leanings, or areas of social concern. Working-class citizens and those below them on the socioeconomic scale usually didn't have the spare time for such things, though informal groups with shared interests would often gather at local pubs or meeting houses for social purposes.<br /> <br /> While these organizations tended to be strictly segregated based upon sex, there's no reason that a Gothic Victorian club couldn't be notorious (yet oddly alluring) among the moneyed classes for allowing women, non-Anglicans, non-Whites, and--it is rumored--even those of lower social class into its halls. If a Storyteller wanted to run a chronicle based around this concept, with the club itself possibly serving as a Chantry, The Kerberos Club from the rpg of the same name is an obvious source for inspiration and adventure ideas. Naturally, adapting the concept to the World of Darkness would require that the club look more like it did early in the century, when the Strange was mostly a matter of whispered rumor, than it did later in the century, when airships were commonplace and magic potions could be ordered through a steampunk version of the internet.<br /> <br /> Among the Traditions on the Council at the time, the Order of Hermes seems the most poised to be involved in the club system, with membership particularly strong in those organizations focused on areas of academic and esoteric interest. Some clubs may serve as little more than places for their members to indulge in sybaritic and Dionysian excesses forbidden by both law and society, which would be a draw for Seers of Chronos/Cultists of Ecstasy. Disparates who make up the Victorian equivalent of Hollow Ones could probably be found among the membership of literary and artistic clubs, as well as various bohemian societies. Celestial Choristers and Euthanatoi would belong for their own reasons, likely professional and social ones. As these clubs at their worst tend to represent a culture that is currently trampling over indigenous populations of several other nations while simultaneously destroying pristine woodlands and belching industrial smoke into the air at home, both the Verbena and the Dreamspeakers seem unlikely candidates at first glance. On the other hand, spiritualists and mediums often count themselves among the Dreamspeakers, and the more successful of them would often be accepted into some of the more broad-minded clubs. Verbena who do have reasons to join would likely belong to clubs focused around their profession, particularly those in the medical and naturalist fields, and those devoted to outdoor pursuits and a healthy lifestyle. I have to admit that I'm drawing a blank when it comes to Akashics. If anything, I could see a club member awakening subsequent to joining, but I can't picture one wanting to join a club unless they had to do so for social cover, or as a specific part of a much larger goal on behalf of the Tradition itself. That's not to say that there is no reason, simply that I'm not coming up with one right now.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union is undoubtedly woven in with the club system, and likely runs more than a few of them while exerting enormous influence over many others. The Invisible Exchequer/Syndicate in particular would be in a position to take credit for the Victorian era explosion of clubs, as this was the result of a newly prosperous and growing upper middle class finding ways to associate with with those of similar financial means after having been turned away from the elite clubs for the upper class and nobility. The Lightkeepers (that was the NWO at this point, if I'm remembering correctly) would likely be found just about everywhere one could find useful information or influence the paradigm, and that would cover nearly every club in Mayfair. Those who have the time, resources, and the correct recommendations and prerequisites for membership would likely belong to several. Explorators/Void Engineers are likely so tied in with Explorer's clubs that membership in one or more is an unspoken necessity for advancement and reputation. They'd also probably be found in the clubs for military officers, particularly ones favored by those who have seen foreign service. The Electrodyne Engineers, the Analytical Reckoners/Virtual Adepts, Aesculpian Order, and whatever Iteration X was at the time (looked it up: International Brotherhood Of Mechanicians. Cute.) most likely belong to a few clubs and societies for scientific advancement, with significant overlap between all four Conventions in each of them. As the general decor of Society of Ether chantries is often portrayed as resembling a British club, it can probably be safely assumed that this aspect of Victorian society was of immense importance in their development as a Convention, and later a Tradition.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the rambling. I've had these ideas rattling around in my head for quite a while, and as I don't currently have the opportunity to game due to other, more vital priorities, I haven't found the motivation to write them down till now. Whether anyone finds the idea useful or not, I'm grateful for the opportunity to finally put these rough ideas out there. There are plenty more, but I'll pace myself for everyone's sake.<br /> <br /> EDIT: While the history of the Victorian era is rife with various esoteric fraternal orders, occult lodges, mystery cults, and spiritualist societies, I'm treating them as separate in type and purpose from the social clubs of the sort mentioned here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25574,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","user":"Heinrich Mentius","date":". 05-16-2021, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T17:54:58-07:00","id":1448732,"title":"","content":"Read the book &quot;Sacred Manhood&quot;. However you treat the book's thesis generally the simple fact that fraternal organizations were a major part of pre-depression era America is indisputable. The Mason's, the Lions Club, the Elks, the Shriners, are but faint remnants of what once was. <br /> American fraternal organizations tended to embrace ritual and drama, a grand place for Hermetics. You could spin the decline of such organizations as a Technocratic plot easily as economic and cultural changed of the sort that the Union supports did cause the decline in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T18:24:51-07:00","id":1448737,"title":"","content":"The Order of the Eastern Star, established as appendant/auxiliary branches of the Masons (originally in the 1850s and fully accepted by the 1870s), also existed, and makes an interesting thing for female Hermetics and other &quot;high ritual&quot; or religious oriented mages (certain members of the Chorus, Verbena, or Dreamspeakers come to mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T18:32:38-07:00","id":1448739,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that one could probably do an entire sourcebook about Egypt and its influence during the Victorian era. Not just the history and politics of what's been happening there since the Napoleonic Wars, but the sudden explosion of Egyptology and interest in ancient Egypt that happened in its wake, and the influence this would've had on the Hermetics and other groups, the resurgence of minor sects like the Children of Osiris, and the like. Do a brief overview of the Traditions in Egypt, and maybe include a cabal based around one of the Museums in London. Also a brief look at what mummies are doing in the Victorian era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T06:35:34-07:00","id":1448770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1448739#post1448739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that one could probably do an entire sourcebook about Egypt and its influence during the Victorian era. Not just the history and politics of what's been happening there since the Napoleonic Wars, but the sudden explosion of Egyptology and interest in ancient Egypt that happened in its wake, and the influence this would've had on the Hermetics and other groups, the resurgence of minor sects like the Children of Osiris, and the like. Do a brief overview of the Traditions in Egypt, and maybe include a cabal based around one of the Museums in London. Also a brief look at what mummies are doing in the Victorian era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, Egyptomania was huge throughout Victoria's reign. India, Tibet, and China, were becoming more fashionable toward the end of the century and all things Native American were big in the Occult circles of America. Cetiomania was huge at the beginning and end of the period. Still Egypt meant magic and mystery throughout the period. <br /> <br /> Although it is now seen as an insult, the term &quot;gypsy&quot; was originally used by the Rom to gain respect by associating themselves with Egypt. The word &quot;sham&quot; for fraud or lie, and the word &quot;shammy&quot; for a cleaning rag, both refer to the &quot;Al Shams&quot; a major grimoire concerned with magic number squares and treasure hunting. The book was authored by an Early Modern Egyptian Arab and used number squares to distract powerful jinn so that ancient Egyptian tombs could be safely robbed.<br /> <br /> Without some knowledge of Egyptomania most of the Victorian occult is indecipherable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T12:56:58-07:00","id":1448798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445490-victorian-mage-expansion-ideas-requests?p=1448770#post1448770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, Egyptomania was huge throughout Victoria's reign. India, Tibet, and China, were becoming more fashionable toward the end of the century and all things Native American were big in the Occult circles of America. Cetiomania was huge at the beginning and end of the period. Still Egypt meant magic and mystery throughout the period.<br /> <br /> Although it is now seen as an insult, the term &quot;gypsy&quot; was originally used by the Rom to gain respect by associating themselves with Egypt. The word &quot;sham&quot; for fraud or lie, and the word &quot;shammy&quot; for a cleaning rag, both refer to the &quot;Al Shams&quot; a major grimoire concerned with magic number squares and treasure hunting. The book was authored by an Early Modern Egyptian Arab and used number squares to distract powerful jinn so that ancient Egyptian tombs could be safely robbed.<br /> <br /> Without some knowledge of Egyptomania most of the Victorian occult is indecipherable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. The Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn often looked like the cast of Cleopatra. Egypt itself must be a hotbed of intrigue between Order of Hermes relic hunters, Technocratic colonial agents trying to take control of the local consensus while shipping the country's heritage to the British Museum, and local Batini and other native Magi trying their best to fight off this invasion of vultures and jackals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T08:26:06-07:00","id":1448865,"title":"","content":"IIRC didn't the sphere system itself arise in part from Egyptian learning - so the re-discovery and promotion of those teachings might become a major plot point in and of itself since it's also foundational to the rise of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> FWIW I always wanted to see Sorcerer's crusade as more 'transitional' between what we know of the Dark Ages magical society and its practices and the new. As I recall the sphere system was relatively new and despite being a better approach to magic than foundation/pillars not everyone would have embraced it (or even heard of it) so you could still have plenty of the 'archaic' means of doing magic (I always thought the minor spheres option from the Storyteller's handbook was a good way to depict 'transitional' magic between foundations and spheres. Although I could see using alternate 'mage' systems introduced in games like Werewolf or Hunter as a lesser variation. Or heck, adapting Awakening's Arcana.) it would take some time for the spheres to proliferate through the magical community and become a standard so you could see lots of variations or distortions of the system. Heck, the institution of the systems that become the bedrock of the modern Mage game can be a big part of what happens during Sorcerer's Crusade.<br /> <br /> In that sense it becomes a 'Crusade' to expand ideas and (for some) an attempt to re-take reality from those who have made it more static for the Traditions, whilst the Order seeks to evolve its own goals and eventually grows into what we know as the Technocracy. The latter one actually has the potential to be more nuanced at that, since there are definite upsides AND downsides to the Technocratic Union's rise (the goal to protect and elevate humanity via reason and science isn't bad in and of itself, but some of the methods and beliefs that outcome fosters are dubious.) <br /> <br /> Sorcerer's Crusade also seems a good time for a 'transition' between the the silent Founts and the prominence of Daemons (Avatars). Some will be seeing them, not everyone may understand what they are or what they represent and that can reflect a huge challenge all its own as well. Many may not still hear them whereas others may hear it and realize there is a new 'way' to evolve their abilities, and still yet others may struggle to come to terms with the Avatar and fail. Some may go crazy others may be seen as 'possesssed' etc. Perhaps not all the psychopomps have vanished yet either, and this decline may be noticed by some in the magical community and now they have to grapple with the challenges that disappearance creates and/or attempt to discover why this is happening. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 05-18-2021, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T08:38:58-07:00","id":1448867,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: making Sorcerer's Crusade transitional from Dark Ages to modern would have required time travel. Because Dark Ages Mage wasn't even a glimmer in the eye of developers who hadn't even been hired yet when Sorcerer's Crusade was written.<br /> <br /> That said, check out the World of Darkness link in my signature. In particular, the first part has a quartet of entries involving the Traditions, the Technocracy, the Disparates, and Orphans, respectively. And they're built around a similar philosophy to the one you just espoused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T10:50:25-07:00","id":1448879,"title":"","content":"An exploration of the Traditions and the Enightened in America in the Victorian Era would probably require its own sourcebook along the lines of Castle Falkenstein's <i>Six-Guns And Sorcery</i>, but I'm hoping to explore a few items that would involve them while not getting lost in the weeds. Called &quot;The Gilded Age&quot; in America (from the title of the Mark Twain book of the same name), this era took America from being an agricultural former colony of the British Empire to being something much closer to the industrial and economic powerhouse we see in the 20th century. Even focusing specifically on the latter half of the century, we see enormous technological, social, and cultural changes, ones that simultaneously grow the economy and fund the drive to find and exploit even more resources. A number of issues and events from the time are likely enormously influenced by the Conventions and Traditions, and have equal or greater influence upon them. I'll explore one defining concept here, and probably some more later.<br /> <br /> <b>Manifest Destiny </b><br /> <br /> The idea that the United States had not just a duty to expand its territory and culture to include all of North America, but was destined to do so, is so inextricably intertwined with Technocratic interests at the time that it's impossible to tell if the Union came up with the concept in the first place, or if they simply took advantage of a popular creed among the unenlightened masses. It is almost certain that if the belief did not originate with them, then they would have come up with something similar. The fortunes of the Technocrats, as well as the expansion of their hold on the consensus, goes hand-in-hand with American expansion and the removal of native tribes from their lands. Mines for coal, silver, and gold are dug on the site of ancient nodes. Oil wells draw Quintessence from sites sacred to the original inhabitants. For an ambitious young Technocrat, the risks of meeting's one demise at the hands of a Dreamspeaker Reality Deviant or a crazed Lycanthrope could be far outweighed by the enormous rewards. It should be remembered, though, that this concept was not universally approved of among the populace, even if it was a prime factor in the growth of the nation.<br /> <br /> The 1800s are arguably the most consequential period for the Conventions since the Renaissance. The Explorators may have outlined the continent itself, but there are still endless miles of untamed (though hardly uninhabited) wilderness yet to be explored by members of the Convention, ones that may contain creatures and beliefs not in line with the Consensus. As they expand the Union's grip, they leave behind flags, forts, and barbed wire to claim and to establish territory gained for the Union. With them or close behind come missionaries and teachers of the Lightkeepers, setting up missions and schools designed to &quot;civilize&quot; the indigenous people into accepting the Technocratic paradigm while back East their newspapers trumpet &quot;Go West, young man!&quot; to implore even further settlement of the conquered regions. When the Indigenous tribes prove resistant to these methods, or are found to be in possession of potentially powerful nodes, the Lightkeepers are willing to employ the most ruthless of methods to remove them from their lands, or even to erase the existence of the population if deemed necessary. Difference Engineers string telegraph and later telephone wires across the continent, and it's only a matter of time before some bright young thing wonders what will happen if you use this technology to connect a Babbage Machine in London to one in San Francisco, and then link them to a third one in Bangladesh. Individual members of the International Brotherhood of Mechanicians, the Electrodyne Engineers, and the Aesculpian Order often provide support to the first waves of Technocratic Explorers with Enlightened weaponry, defenses, and medical technology, then use the now-uninhabited regions to set up laboratories far from the unenlightened masses where they can experiment with less risk of paradoxical backlash. The railroad eventually links one coast to the other due largely to their efforts, but at the sacrifice of countless Asian and Black railroad workers who suffered endless abuse, exploitation, and death, possibly at the design of Syndicate operatives looking to gain maximum labor for minimum investment. The drive West has been entirely funded through their largesse, and they expect a return upon their investment. This pays off beyond all belief in with the gold and silver rushes of the era, though it also leads to economic calamity for many due to inflation and price-gouging.<br /> <br /> Among the Traditions, one thing is constant through the entirety of this century and beyond: The Dreamspeakers are justifiably <i>pissed</i>. Their nodes are being co-opted and destroyed, the spirits no longer speak to them as readily as they once did, their hold on the consensus is disappearing from the few cultures where it still held strong, and their people are being rapidly eliminated through slaughter, disease, and the poisoning of their lands. I can't see the Council as providing any sort of unified front against the expansion, either, as each Tradition is dealing with their own issues right now, or (in one or two cases) may even see this as an opportunity for further power. A number of Akashics probably make it over with the railroad workers, but perhaps can also be found among the devotees of popular exercise regimens and dietary fads such as those of John Harvey Kellogg. Later on, they probably establish a significant presence in San Francisco, along with their rivals in the Wu Lung. The Batini are fighting a hopeless war over their most sacred places, and even sympathetic ones are probably not in a position to offer significant assistance, though there's nothing to prevent them from sending representatives to find common cause with the natives. Euthanatoi ride the plains as dispensers of justice in a lawless land, and make a living at the poker tables of western saloons. A few likely serve as soldiers, Sheriffs, U.S. Marshals, and bounty hunters. Ecstatics run religious &quot;free love&quot; communes in areas far enough from the cities to not attract the attention of the law, work as entertainers and/or prostitutes in taverns from St. Louis to San Francisco, and fulfill the societal role of the town drunk in more than one settler community. The Celestial Chorus is split among its membership: While they deplore the violence against the indigenous people (and the resultant tragedy befalling their colleagues on the Council), could this not also be seen by some as an opportunity to spread the word of the One, and to bring those currently suffering to His Divine Presence? Most of the modern generation is likely horrified by this perspective, but I can see it as having a strong enough hold among the leadership for them to take a hands-off approach while still allowing individual Choristers to follow their conscience. Of course, long before the land was settled by Europeans, there were Native Choristers whose beliefs in a Great Mystery (or &quot;Great Spirit,&quot; as it's popularly known) would cause many in the Tradition to see this as a shared struggle. Choristers serve as missionaries and traveling preachers (such as John Chapman, better known as &quot;Johnny Appleseed&quot;), but also as temperance activists, poets, and traveling musicians and singers, Among the Verbena, even those who are not among the Native tribes would probably be instinctively repulsed by the wholesale slaughter of the indigenous people, the decimation of the wildlife and the toxic exploitation of the land's natural resources. Popular professions and concepts would likely include medicine show peddlers, midwives, cooks, local wise women, and guides through the wilderness. Within the Order of Hermes, an entirely different perspective holds sway: As the Order does much of its American recruitment through the mystic lodges and occult orders that attract many who have extensive financial stakes in the expansion, they may see this as an opportunity to be exploited. After all, their reasoning goes, if the Dreamspeakers can't use their talents and primitive hedge magic to defend what is theirs, then what good is it? If they're doing nothing with their nodes to advance their knowledge or their power, then why should they have them in the first place? The only problem is that the power is falling into the hands of the Technocracy, but if the order moves fast enough, they may be able to keep a large number of places and items of power far from their reach. it's a shame that so many Natives have to die, but such is ever the price of knowledge. Naturally, not all Order members share this inhuman view, but not nearly enough of them to make a difference in the Tradition. Order of Hermes members are usually found among the more educated settlers, such as schoolteachers, professors, doctors, ministers, anthropologists, naturalists, and military officers.<br /> <br /> Forgive any unclear passages, disjointed ideas, or awkward verbiage. I only had about half of this in mind when I started writing, and it became more unwieldly as I thought of new ideas while I was in the process of writing down the original thoughts. I also have some ideas on Gilded Age New York and the Civil War, but this is more than enough for a single post.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Forgot to mention: The history of Hawaii during this time is also a result of this belief in Manifest Destiny, as mentioned upthread, but as my only familiarity with the topic is through my having read Sarah Vowell's Unfamiliar Fishes shortly after it was first published over a decade ago, I'll leave that story to those with greater familiarity with it than myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25574,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","user":"Heinrich Mentius","date":". 05-18-2021, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T11:15:36-07:00","id":1448882,"title":"","content":"<i>Apologies. Accidentally posted here when I meant to edit the previous post. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T13:30:15-07:00","id":1456150,"title":"","content":"I may be a bit late but...<br /> <br /> Russia is a perfect spot. It had it all. It was a setting where almost every tradition would find its place. A place of many religions, which would form a base of strength of Celestial Chorus and even Dream Speakers (shamanism was, and to this day is, common in Siberian tribes) and a melting pot of nations, which resulted in political turmoil. There was an advancing civilization with modern (well - more or less) cities, booming industry centres like \u0141\u00f3d\u017a, feats of engineering like Trans-Siberian Railway but also a very backward province, where the things have been the same for centuries (as were the old spells and miracles). There were the newly conquered territories of Central Asia where the the nomads roamed like their forefathers while the new cities rose. There were the secret cabals and occultism in aristocratic groups and there were yurodivys - sacred madmen typical to Rus (which is a very interesting concept for a chorister or maybe an ecstatic). There was a frontier in Far East with the mix of various races and religions (so even the Akashic could fit in). Reality Zones would change from place to place much more than in the West and the Reason is likely to keep battling against the Faith (or maybe Faiths) and Magic. That battle is going to be harder than in other places in Europe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26990-siegfried","name":"Siegfried","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T18:22:57-07:00","id":1456158,"title":"","content":"In the same vein Indonesia ( The Dutch East Indies in period) has many similar qualities. Many small island sultanates were effectively lost in time in our world. Bali had the local gods and spirits processing people in the public streets and it was accepted as normal. Not only Mage could be expanded here, some of the East Indies would be in the Near Dreaming. On some Islands the gauntlet would be so weak that you could walk through to the Umbra by accident. <br /> <br /> The only problem is getting good source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}